<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10978" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conventīcĭus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tītĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		convenio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>pertaining to coming together</i>, or <i>intercourse</i>. * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">patres conventicii,</span>”
				<i>coming from various quarters</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cist. 1, 1, 42</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conventī-cĭum</span></b> , ii,
				n. (sc. aes), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ
				ἐκκλησιαστικόν</span>, <i>money paid to the
				poorer Greek citizens for attendance in the assemblies of the
				people</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Rep. 3, 35, 48</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
